{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "830cbea8-a689-484e-9745-43d191c25963",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Calculate depth to water table from the surface from ATS simulation outputs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c3b6370e-f302-41fe-8e1a-52ee9f859cdf",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [],
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "plaintext"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "##### The following script calculates the water table depth from ATS-simulated subsurface pressure.\n",
    "##### It employs a bottom-up approach to identify the last saturated cell starting from the bottom soil layers. In other words, the pressure of the last saturated cell, indexed from the bottom (where the bottom-most subsurface cell has an index of 0), is used to calculate the water table depth.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f3ce151b-9293-4b82-8862-5278990406f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Water Table Depth Formula\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Water_Table_Depth} = z_{\\text{surface}} - z_{\\text{cell}} - \\frac{P_{\\text{cell}} - P_{\\text{atm}}}{\\rho_{\\text{water}} \\cdot g}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Where:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- $z_{\\text{surface}}$, $z_{\\text{cell}}$ are the z coordinates $[m]$ of the surface and the identified last saturated subsurface cell, respectively  \n",
    "- $P_{\\text{cell}}$ is the corresponding cell's subsurface pressure $[Pa]$  \n",
    "- $P_{\\text{atm}}$ is atmospheric pressure (typically $101325\\, Pa$)  \n",
    "- $\\rho_{\\text{water}}$ is the water density (typically $997\\, kg/m^3$)  \n",
    "- $g$ is gravitational acceleration ($9.80665\\, m/s^2$)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8cbb4d9b-c157-4996-9595-5f1cb16f6a71",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### User Inputs ::: \n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "42924946-e451-4ac0-b400-57b48a90eedf",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the output model directory, where ats_vis_data.h5, ats_vis_mesh.h5, ats_vis_surface_data.h5 and ats_vis_surface_mesh.h5 are located\n",
    "model_dir = '/path to the ATS output folder/'\n",
    "# Define the following Parameters AND verify their consistency with the XML\n",
    "rho = 997 # density of water, kg m^-3\n",
    "g = 9.80665 # gravity, m s^-2\n",
    "patm = 101325 # atmopsheric pressure, Pascals"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d423937e-ffc6-4d10-9b6c-8209d5110e08",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Loading necessary pacakges"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "53d0b1ad-c0c5-48b5-829d-f5415055945c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys,os\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.join(os.environ['ATS_SRC_DIR'],'tools', 'utils'))\n",
    "import ats_xdmf\n",
    "import numpy as np "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b13430b6-bd5b-4e69-81d6-c0de91f3d138",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "### Function to estimate WTD based on pressure "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "87dd0bc4-3e2b-4883-8740-9f536b3cd49e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def map_surface_subsurface_ats_ids(visfile_surface, visfile_subsurface, decimal_rounding=4):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Matches surface and subsurface cell IDs based on (x, y) centroid coordinates.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters\n",
    "    ----------\n",
    "    visfile_surface : VisFile\n",
    "        ATS VisFile object for surface domain, with .centroids of shape (n, 3)\n",
    "    visfile_subsurface : VisFile\n",
    "        ATS VisFile object for subsurface domain, with .centroids of shape (n, k, 3)\n",
    "    decimal_rounding : int, optional\n",
    "        Number of decimal places to round coordinates for matching (default is 4)\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns\n",
    "    -------\n",
    "    surface_subsurface_IDs : np.ndarray\n",
    "        (n, 2) array where each row is (surface_index, matched_subsurface_index)\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    surface_xy = np.round(visfile_surface.centroids[:, :2], decimal_rounding)\n",
    "    subsurface_xy = np.round(visfile_subsurface.centroids[:, 0, :2], decimal_rounding)\n",
    "\n",
    "    surface_view = surface_xy.view([('x', 'f8'), ('y', 'f8')])\n",
    "    subsurface_view = subsurface_xy.view([('x', 'f8'), ('y', 'f8')])\n",
    "\n",
    "    sort_idx = np.argsort(subsurface_view.ravel())\n",
    "    subsurface_sorted = subsurface_view.ravel()[sort_idx]\n",
    "    surface_matches = np.searchsorted(subsurface_sorted, surface_view.ravel())\n",
    "    matched_subsurface_indices = sort_idx[surface_matches]\n",
    "\n",
    "    surface_indices = np.arange(surface_xy.shape[0])\n",
    "    surface_subsurface_IDs = np.column_stack((surface_indices, matched_subsurface_indices))\n",
    "\n",
    "    assert np.allclose(\n",
    "        surface_xy, subsurface_xy[matched_subsurface_indices]\n",
    "    ), f\"Coordinate mismatch: try a different rounding precision (currently {decimal_rounding})\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    return surface_subsurface_IDs\n",
    "    \n",
    "def get_ats_wtd_pressurebased(pressure_subsurface,visfile_surface, visfile_subsurface, surface_subsurface_IDs=None):\n",
    "    iz_coord = visfile_subsurface.centroids[:,:,-1]\n",
    "\n",
    "    if surface_subsurface_IDs is None:\n",
    "        surface_subsurface_IDs = map_surface_subsurface_ats_ids(visfile_surface, visfile_subsurface)\n",
    "\n",
    "    ### Estimate WTD based on pressure\n",
    "    # pressure head\n",
    "    ih = (pressure_subsurface - patm) / (rho * g)\n",
    "    mask = ih > 0\n",
    "    first_false_idx = (~mask).argmax(axis=-1)\n",
    "    max_len = mask.shape[-1]\n",
    "    indices = np.arange(max_len)\n",
    "    mask2 = indices < first_false_idx[..., np.newaxis]\n",
    "    all_true_rows = (first_false_idx == 0)\n",
    "    mask2[all_true_rows] = True\n",
    "    sat_idx = mask2[:, :, ::-1].argmax(axis=-1)\n",
    "    sat_idx = mask2.shape[-1] - 1 - sat_idx\n",
    "    sat_idx[~mask2.any(axis=-1)] = 0\n",
    "    # WTD elevation\n",
    "    iH_rev = ih[np.arange(ih.shape[0])[:, None], np.arange(ih.shape[1]), sat_idx] + iz_coord[np.arange(ih.shape[1]), sat_idx] \n",
    "    first_depth_to_centroid = visfile_surface.centroids[surface_subsurface_IDs[0][0], -1] - visfile_subsurface.centroids[surface_subsurface_IDs[0][1], -1, -1]\n",
    "    # WTD (from surface)\n",
    "    wtd_pressure_based = np.maximum(iz_coord[:,-1]+first_depth_to_centroid - iH_rev, 0) \n",
    "    assert pressure_subsurface[:,:,1].shape == wtd_pressure_based.shape, f\"Shape mismatch: Error in WTD calculation\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    ### Re-arrange WTD in accordance to surface IDs\n",
    "    # As pressure obtained from subsurface does not follow surface ID, re-arrange this:\n",
    "    wtd_pressure_rearranged = wtd_pressure_based[:, surface_subsurface_IDs[:, 1]]\n",
    "    # wtd_pressure_rearranged can now be directly compared with array obtained from visfile_surface.getArray('surface-water_table_depth')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return wtd_pressure_rearranged, surface_subsurface_IDs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f4d0933d-012e-4b60-ab27-c132545cb136",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Get WTD"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "12200cfd-108f-430f-9045-2f5a0f0615a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "visfile_subsurface = ats_xdmf.VisFile(model_dir, time_unit='d')\n",
    "visfile_subsurface.loadMesh(columnar=True)\n",
    "# loading surface mesh file\n",
    "visfile_surface = ats_xdmf.VisFile(model_dir, domain='surface', time_unit='d')\n",
    "visfile_surface.loadMesh()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "2474db7b-2494-464f-bf2b-d5952557793f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
